rty. Ancient Rome upheld it as a sign of power and victory. Throughout history, this bird has symbolized the courage to break bonds, overcome adversity, and feast on the fullness of life. \\\",\\\"Like the Penguin, at home on land or in the sea, we live in two worlds—the solid, waking world of the everyday and the deep ocean of the unconscious, where dreams live and stories are born.\\\",\\\"The wise Owl brings magic and ancient knowledge out of the dark and into the moonlight. It represents our comfort in the strange, quiet places where mystery waits.\\\"];\\n\"\n ]\n}"